# Python Pipeline Validation & Data Quality Monitoring Framework

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates how Python can support data engineering and BI teams by monitoring pipeline reliability, data quality, and reporting readiness across an Azure-based data platform.

The workflow represents a real-world analytics environment where business users define reporting needs, Jira and Confluence are used for requirements and documentation, Azure Data Factory orchestrates ingestion, SHIR supports on-prem/SAP connectivity, ADLS Gen2 stores raw data, Databricks transforms data through Silver and Gold layers, and curated outputs are consumed in Power BI or Tableau.

## Business Context

Business users rely on dashboards for KPI tracking, reporting, and decision-making. If upstream pipelines fail, run late, load zero records, or produce mismatched data, downstream reports can become inaccurate.

This framework helps identify those issues before the data is trusted for reporting.

## End-to-End Flow

```text
Business Users / Stakeholders
        ↓
Business requirements, KPIs, reporting needs
        ↓
Jira / Confluence
User stories, documentation, acceptance criteria, validation rules
        ↓
Data Engineering Team
Technical requirements and pipeline implementation
        ↓
Source Systems
SAP / on-prem systems / enterprise databases
        ↓
Azure Data Factory
Pipeline orchestration
        ↓
Lookup Activity
Reads metadata/control table for load instructions
        ↓
Copy Activity + SHIR
Moves data from SAP/on-prem systems through Self-Hosted Integration Runtime
        ↓
ADLS Gen2 Bronze Layer
Raw data lands as-is
        ↓
Databricks Silver Layer
Data cleaning, standardization, validation
        ↓
Databricks Gold Layer
Business-ready curated datasets
        ↓
Azure SQL / Synapse
Structured downstream reporting layer
        ↓
Power BI / Tableau
Dashboards, KPI tracking, ad hoc analysis, and business insights
